<title>UK: ICI falls on profit-taking, ADR weakness.</title>
<headline>ICI falls on profit-taking, ADR weakness.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Imperial Chemical Industries Plc on profit-taking, after the company's ADRs weakened overnight, dealers said.</p>
<p>The shares were down 20p to 835 at 1101 GMT after the ADRs lost $1 to close at $56-3/4 in New York.</p>
<p>&quot;The stock has had a good run,&quot; said one market maker. &quot;They've gone from about seven pounds up in a straight line.&quot;</p>
<p>The shares have climbed 23 percent from May 2 to their recent high at 863 on June 10.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
